UM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tLogin share\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\twifi_web_auth_applet_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tWifi web auth\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tmy_page_applet_mode\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECustom frontend\u001F1\u001EReal applet\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tMy page\t\u0001\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tLibraryApplet\tenable_overlay\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tEnable Overlay Applet\tEnables Horizon\\'s built-in overlay applet. Press and hold the home button for 1 second to show it.\tLibrary Applet\neden\t\u0001\tAudio\toutput_engine\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001ECubeb\u001F2\u001ESdl2\u001F3\u001ENull\u001F4\u001EOboe\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tOutput Engine\t\u0001\tAudio\neden\t\u0001\tSystem\tsound_index\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EMono\u001F1\u001EStereo\u001F2\u001ESurround\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSound Output Mode\t\u0001\tSystem Audio\neden\t\u0001\tAudio\tvolume\tINT\t100\t0\t200\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tVolume\t\u0001\tAudio\neden\t\u0001\tAudio\taudio_muted\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tMute audio\t\u0001\tAudio\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tuse_multi_core\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tMulticore CPU Emulation\tThis option increases CPU emulation thread use from 1 to the maximum of 4. This is mainly a debug option and shouldn't be disabled.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tuse_speed_limit\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tspeed_limit\tINT\t100\t0\t9999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tLimit Speed Percent\tControls the game's maximum rendering speed, but it's up to each game if it runs faster or not. 200% for a 30 FPS game is 60 FPS, and for a 60 FPS game it will be 120 FPS. Disabling it means unlocking the framerate to the maximum your PC can reach.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tslow_speed_limit\tINT\t50\t0\t9999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tSlow Speed\tWhen the Slow Speed hotkey is pressed, the speed will be limited to this percentage.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tturbo_speed_limit\tINT\t200\t0\t9999\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tTurbo Speed\tWhen the Turbo Speed hotkey is pressed, the speed will be limited to this percentage.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCore\tsync_core_speed\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSynchronize Core Speed\tSynchronizes CPU core speed with the game's maximum rendering speed to boost FPS without affecting game speed (animations, physics, etc.). Can help reduce stuttering at lower framerates.\tCore\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpu_accuracy\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001EAccurate\u001F2\u001EUnsafe\u001F3\u001EParanoid (disables most optimizations)\u001F4\u001EDebugging\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tAccuracy\tChange the accuracy of the emulated CPU (for debugging only).\tCpu\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tfast_cpu_time\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F1\u001EBoost (1700MHz)\u001F2\u001EFast) ENUM(MemoryLayout\u001F3\u001EMemory_4Gb\u001F4\u001EMemory_6Gb\u001F5\u001EMemory_8Gb\u001F6\u001EMemory_10Gb\u001F7\u001EMemory_12Gb\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tCPU Overclock\tOverclocks the emulated CPU to remove some FPS limiters. Weaker CPUs may see reduced performance, and certain games may behave improperly. Use Boost (1700MHz) to run at the Switch's highest native clock, or Fast (2000MHz) to run at 2x clock.\tCpu\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tuse_custom_cpu_ticks\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpu_ticks\tINT\t16000\t77\t65535\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tCustom CPU Ticks\tSet a custom value of CPU ticks. Higher values can increase performance, but may cause deadlocks. A range of 77-21000 is recommended.\tCpu\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_page_tables\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_block_linking\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_return_stack_buffer\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_fast_dispatcher\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_context_elimination\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_const_prop\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_misc_ir\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_reduce_misalign_checks\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_fastmem\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_fastmem_exclusives\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_recompile_exclusives\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_ignore_memory_aborts\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tCpu Debug\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_unfuse_fma\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tUnfuse FMA (improve performance on CPUs without FMA)\tThis option improves speed by reducing accuracy of fused-multiply-add instructions on CPUs without native FMA support.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_reduce_fp_error\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFaster FRSQRTE and FRECPE\tThis option improves the speed of some approximate floating-point functions by using less accurate native approximations.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_ignore_standard_fpcr\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFaster ASIMD instructions (32 bits only)\tThis option improves the speed of 32 bits ASIMD floating-point functions by running with incorrect rounding modes.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_inaccurate_nan\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tInaccurate NaN handling\tThis option improves speed by removing NaN checking. Please note this also reduces accuracy of certain floating-point instructions.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_fastmem_check\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tDisable address space checks\tThis option improves speed by eliminating a safety check before every memory operation. Disabling it may allow arbitrary code execution.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tCpu\tcpuopt_unsafe_ignore_global_monitor\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tIgnore global monitor\tThis option improves speed by relying only on the semantics of cmpxchg to ensure safety of exclusive access instructions. Please note this may result in deadlocks and other race conditions.\tCpu Unsafe\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tvulkan_device\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tDevice\tThis setting selects the GPU to use (Vulkan only).\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tresolution_setup\tENUM\t3\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001E0.25X (180p/270p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F1\u001E0.5X (360p/540p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F2\u001E0.75X (540p/810p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F3\u001E1X (720p/1080p)\u001F4\u001E1.25X (900p/1350p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F5\u001E1.5X (1080p/1620p) [EXPERIMENTAL]\u001F6\u001E2X (1440p/2160p)\u001F7\u001E3X (2160p/3240p)\u001F8\u001E4X (2880p/4320p)\u001F9\u001E5X (3600p/5400p)\u001F10\u001E6X (4320p/6480p)\u001F11\u001E7X (5040p/7560p)\u001F12\u001E8X (5760p/8640p)\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tResolution\tForces to render at a different resolution. Higher resolutions require more VRAM and bandwidth. Options lower than 1X can cause artifacts.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_vsync\tENUM\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EImmediate\u001F1\u001EMailbox\u001F2\u001EFifo\u001F3\u001EFifoRelaxed\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tVSync Mode\tFIFO (VSync) does not drop frames or exhibit tearing but is limited by the screen refresh rate. FIFO Relaxed allows tearing as it recovers from a slow down. Mailbox can have lower latency than FIFO and does not tear but may drop frames. Immediate (no synchronization) presents whatever is available and can exhibit tearing.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tscaling_filter\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENearest Neighbor\u001F1\u001EBilinear\u001F2\u001EBicubic\u001F3\u001EGaussian\u001F4\u001ELanczos\u001F5\u001EScaleForce\u001F6\u001EAMD FidelityFX Super Resolution\u001F7\u001EArea\u001F8\u001EZero-Tangent\u001F9\u001EB-Spline\u001F10\u001EMitchell\u001F11\u001ESpline-1\u001F12\u001EMMPX\u001F13\u001EMaxEnum\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tWindow Adapting Filter\t\u0001\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tfsr_sharpening_slider\tINT\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFSR Sharpness\tDetermines how sharpened the image will look using FSR's dynamic contrast.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\taspect_ratio\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDefault (16:9)\u001F1\u001EForce 4:3\u001F2\u001EForce 21:9\u001F3\u001EForce 16:10\u001F4\u001EStretch to Window\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tAspect Ratio\tStretches the renderer to fit the specified aspect ratio. Most games only support 16:9, so modifications are required to get other ratios. Also controls the aspect ratio of captured screenshots.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tanti_aliasing\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENone\u001F1\u001EFXAA\u001F2\u001ESMAA\u001F3\u001EMaxEnum\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tAnti-Aliasing Method\tThe anti-aliasing method to use. SMAA offers the best quality. FXAA can produce a more stable picture in lower resolutions.\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbg_red\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbg_green\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbg_blue\tINT\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdma_accuracy\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EDefault\u001F1\u001EUnsafe (fast)\u001F2\u001ESafe (stable)\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tDMA Accuracy\tControls the DMA precision accuracy. Safe precision fixes issues in some games but may degrade performance.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tvram_usage_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EConservative\u001F1\u001EAggressive\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tVRAM Usage Mode\tSelects whether the emulator should prefer to conserve memory or make maximum usage of available video memory for performance. Aggressive mode may impact performance of other applications such as recording software.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tnvdec_emulation\tENUM\t2\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ENo Video Output\u001F1\u001ECPU Video Decoding\u001F2\u001EGPU Video Decoding (Default)\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tNVDEC emulation\tSpecifies how videos should be decoded. It can either use the CPU or the GPU for decoding, or perform no decoding at all (black screen on videos). In most cases, GPU decoding provides the best performance.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\taccelerate_astc\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001ECPU\u001F1\u001EGPU\u001F2\u001ECPU Asynchronous\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tASTC Decoding Method\tThis option controls how ASTC textures should be decoded. CPU: Use the CPU for decoding. GPU: Use the GPU's compute shaders to decode ASTC textures (recommended). CPU Asynchronously: Use the CPU to decode ASTC textures on demand. EliminatesASTC decoding stuttering but may present artifacts.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tframe_pacing_mode\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EAuto\u001F1\u001E30 FPS\u001F2\u001E60 FPS\u001F3\u001E90 FPS\u001F4\u001E120 FPS\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tFrame Pacing Mode (Vulkan only)\tControls how the emulator manages frame pacing to reduce stuttering and make the frame rate smoother and more consistent.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tastc_recompression\tENUM\t0\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EUncompressed (Best quality)\u001F1\u001EBC1 (Low quality)\u001F2\u001EBC3 (Medium quality)\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tASTC Recompression Method\tMost GPUs lack support for ASTC textures and must decompress to anintermediate format: RGBA8. BC1/BC3: The intermediate format will be recompressed to BC1 or BC3 format,  saving VRAM but degrading image quality.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tsync_memory_operations\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSync Memory Operations\tEnsures data consistency between compute and memory operations. This option fixes issues in games, but may degrade performance. Unreal Engine 4 games often see the most significant changes thereof.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tforce_max_clock\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tForce maximum clocks (Vulkan only)\tRuns work in the background while waiting for graphics commands to keep the GPU from lowering its clock speed.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_disk_shader_cache\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tUse persistent pipeline cache\tAllows saving shaders to storage for faster loading on following game boots. Disabling it is only intended for debugging.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_vulkan_driver_pipeline_cache\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tUse Vulkan pipeline cache\tEnables GPU vendor-specific pipeline cache. This option can improve shader loading time significantly in cases where the Vulkan driver does not store pipeline cache files internally.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tenable_compute_pipelines\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tEnable Compute Pipelines (Intel Vulkan Only)\tRequired by some games. This setting only exists for Intel proprietary drivers and may crash if enabled. Compute pipelines are always enabled on all other drivers.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_video_framerate\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSync to framerate of video playback\tRun the game at normal speed during video playback, even when the framerate is unlocked.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tbarrier_feedback_loops\tBOOL\ttrue\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tBarrier feedback loops\tImproves rendering of transparency effects in specific games.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tenable_buffer_history\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tEnable buffer history\tEnables access to previous buffer states. This option may improve rendering quality and performance consistency in some games.\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_optimized_vertex_buffers\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Advanced\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tfast_gpu_time\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EOff\u001F1\u001EMedium (256)\u001F2\u001EHigh) ENUM(GpuUnswizzleSize\u001F3\u001EVerySmall\u001F4\u001ESmall\u001F5\u001EOff\u001F6\u001ELarge\u001F7\u001EVeryLarge) ENUM(GpuUnswizzle\u001F8\u001EVeryLow\u001F9\u001ELow\u001F10\u001EOff\u001F11\u001EMedium (256)\u001F12\u001EHigh) ENUM(GpuUnswizzleChunk\u001F13\u001EVeryLow\u001F14\u001ELow\u001F15\u001EOff\u001F16\u001EMedium (256)\u001F17\u001EHigh) ENUM(TemperatureUnits\u001F18\u001ECelsius\u001F19\u001EFahrenheit) ENUM(ExtendedDynamicState\u001F20\u001EDisabled\u001F21\u001EEDS1\u001F22\u001EEDS2\u001F23\u001EEDS3\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFast GPU Time\tOverclocks the emulated GPU to increase dynamic resolution and render distance. Use 256 for maximal performance and 512 for maximal graphics fidelity.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tskip_cpu_inner_invalidation\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSkip CPU Inner Invalidation\tSkips certain cache invalidations during memory updates, reducing CPU usage and improving latency. This may cause soft-crashes.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tfix_bloom_effects\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tFix bloom effects\tRemoves bloom in Burnout.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\temulate_bgr565\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tuse_asynchronous_shaders\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tEnable asynchronous shader compilation\tMay reduce shader stutter.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tgpu_unswizzle_enabled\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0\tGPU Unswizzle\tAccelerates BCn 3D texture decoding using GPU compute. Disable if experiencing crashes or graphical glitches.\tRenderer Hacks\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tsample_shading_fraction\tINT\t0\t0\t100\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tSample Shading\tAllows the fragment shader to execute per sample in a multi-sampled fragment instead of once per fragment. Improves graphics quality at the cost of performance. Higher values improve quality but degrade performance.\tRenderer Extensions\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdebug\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tshader_feedback\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tnsight_aftermath\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdisable_shader_loop_safety_checks\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\trenderdoc_hotkey\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tpatch_old_qcom_drivers\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t0\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tRenderer\tdisable_buffer_reorder\tBOOL\tfalse\t\u0001\t\u0001\t\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\t\u0001\t\u0001\tRenderer Debug\neden\t\u0001\tSystem\tlanguage_index\tENUM\t1\t\u0001\t\u0001\t0\u001EJapanese (日本語)\u001F1\u001EAmerican English\u001F2\u001EFrench (français)\u001F3\u001EGerman (Deutsch)\u001F4\u001EItalian (italiano)\u001F5\u001ESpanish (español)\u001F6\u001EChinese\u001F7\u001EKorean (한국어)\u001F8\u001EDutch (Nederlands)\u001F9\u001EPortuguese (português)\u001F10\u001ERussian (Русский)\u001F11\u001ETaiwanese\u001F12\u001EBritish English\u001F13\u001ECanadian French\u001F14\u001ELatin American Spanish\u001F15\u001ESimplified Chinese\u001F16\u001ETraditional Chinese (正體中文)\u001F17\u001EBrazilian Portuguese (português do Brasil)\u001F18\u001EPolish (polska)\u001F19\u001EThai (แบบไทย)\t1\t\u0001\tv0.2.1,v0.2.0,v0.1.1,v0.1.0\tLanguage\tThis option can b